The repository is built to be worked on by many Claude Code agents at once, on one or several machines, with
[agent-harness](https://github.com/Marius-Juston/agent-harness) ({{ harness_ref }}).

## Quickstart
```bash
uv run dev setup      # git, uv sync, generated docs, git config, prek hooks, Claude Code plugins; then a doctor report
uv run dev doctor     # what this machine still needs (tools, auth, MCP servers)
claude                # the SessionStart hook prints the handoff, board and machine state
```
Prerequisites: git, [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), [gh](https://cli.github.com) (authenticated), jq, Node.js 20+
(for the Playwright MCP server) and [Claude Code](https://code.claude.com/docs).
Research API keys (free, once per machine, never in the repository): [docs/SETUP.md](docs/SETUP.md#research-api-keys).
To start or continue the work, paste the `/goal` prompt from [docs/SESSION.md](docs/SESSION.md).

## How work flows
- **Board:** GitHub issues with status labels (`uv run dev board list`). Every item has a measurable DONE WHEN.
- **Lead and workers:** the main session leads; subagents of the `harness-ops` plugin each take one issue in their
  own worktree and hand back a gated PR. Only `uv run dev integrate` merges, after re-gating the merged tree.
- **Gate:** `uv run dev check`: drift checks, word budgets, generated docs, lint and tests. CI runs the same command.

## Updating the harness
`uvx copier check-update` says whether a newer agent-harness release exists; `uvx copier update` applies it
(three-way, so local edits are kept), including the pinned devkit and plugin versions. Then `uv sync`. It never
touches CLAUDE.md or this README: the generic agent rules live in `.devkit/HARNESS.md`, which CLAUDE.md @-imports.

What exists is generated, never hand-listed: [docs/generated/agent-surface.md](docs/generated/agent-surface.md).
